Hi Carolyn and Mihoko,

Brian and I settled the 24 July follow-up slots this morning. His attached gr=
id (CWR-DR-20260415-DEC-02 v1.0) reserves twelve slots for people who gave or=
 received a handoff on three or more of their last five worked shifts, and tw=
elve for people who did so on two or fewer. If someone both gave and received=
 a handoff during a shift, count that shift once.

Please don't move a candidate with an unknown count into a slot to even out t=
he country mix. Check the last five shifts first, then place the candidate in=
 the matching frequency group. A confirmed zero belongs in the lower group; a=
n unknown count stays outside both until confirmed.

Use the US and Japan columns to arrange dates with each desk. If someone drop=
s out, look for a replacement in the same frequency group. Leave the intervie=
w numbers and confirmed times for the July records so the reservation grid ca=
n stay in frequency order.

Thanks for coordinating the dates together.
Jennifer

